TITLE='Can last year explain next year’s energy intensity?'
SUBTITLE='Prior-year building attributes → next-year reported EUI'
LIMITS='The eligible cohort requires compliant, active records in both years and usable prior-year floor area and age. Results therefore describe continuing eligible reporters, not all buildings. Property IDs recur across time by design. EUI is weather normalized but this is an observational prediction exercise, not an estimate of retrofit savings. Exclude 2025 pending source metadata review. No uncertainty intervals or deployment claims.'
STYLE='*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#edf3f5;color:#183142;font:16px system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1240px;margin:auto;padding:40px}header{padding:30px;background:#133346;color:white;border-radius:18px}h1{font-size:38px;letter-spacing:-1px;margin:12px 0}h2{font-size:23px}h3{font-size:16px}p{line-height:1.6}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#83d6db}.muted,small{color:#597180}header .muted{color:#bfd1da}section,.panel{background:white;border:1px solid #dce6ea;border-radius:14px;padding:24px;margin-top:22px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:16px}.charts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{padding:22px;background:white;border-radius:14px;border:1px solid #dce6ea}.value{font-size:36px;font-weight:700;margin:10px 0}.filters{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}label{display:grid;gap:8px;font-size:13px}select,button{font:inherit;padding:9px;border:1px solid #bacdd6;border-radius:7px;background:white;color:#183142}a{color:#087d87}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:12px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #e2ebef}th{color:#597180}img{max-width:100%;border-radius:10px}.barrow{margin:15px 0;font-size:13px}.barhead{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px}.track{height:13px;background:#edf3f5;border-radius:3px;margin-top:6px}.fill{height:100%;background:#167f89;border-radius:3px}.notice{border-left:4px solid #b87b2f;background:#fff8ec;padding:15px}.tag{font-size:12px;color:#087d87;font-weight:bold}.footer{font-size:13px;color:#597180;margin:30px 0}code{background:#eaf1f5;padding:3px 6px;border-radius:4px}@media(max-width:800px){main{padding:16px}.grid,.charts{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}@media(max-width:500px){.grid,.charts{grid-template-columns:1fr}}'
from pathlib import Path
import csv,json,html
BASE=Path(__file__).parent
def esc(v):return html.escape(str(v))
def table(path):
    with path.open() as f: rows=list(csv.reader(f))
    return '<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+esc(v)+'</th>' for v in rows[0])+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(v)+'</td>' for v in r)+'</tr>' for r in rows[1:])+'</tbody></table>'
with (BASE/'results/metrics.csv').open() as f: metrics=list(csv.DictReader(f))
hold=[r for r in metrics if r['population']=='2024 holdout'];model,baseline=hold
improvement=100*(float(baseline['MAE'])-float(model['MAE']))/float(baseline['MAE'])
comparison=f"The model's holdout MAE is {float(model['MAE']):,.2f}, compared with {float(baseline['MAE']):,.2f} for the baseline. This is {abs(improvement):.1f}% {'lower' if improvement>=0 else 'higher'} error on the same {int(model['n']):,} observations."
manifest=json.loads((BASE/'data/source-manifest.json').read_text())
body='<header><div class="eyebrow">RStudio / independent public-data portfolio</div><h1>'+TITLE+'</h1><p class="muted">'+SUBTITLE+'</p><small class="muted">City of Seattle public data · Snapshot 20 October 2026 · No client or city affiliation</small></header>'
body+='<section><span class="tag">MEASURED RESULT / 2024 HOLDOUT</span><h2>Does the model beat a simple baseline?</h2><p>'+comparison+'</p><p>MAE is average absolute prediction error; lower is better. Model choices are fixed for this demonstration, with a chronological 2023 development check and a separate 2024 evaluation. These historical results are not a guarantee of future performance.</p>'+table(BASE/'results/metrics.csv')+'</section>'
body+='<section><h2>Stability matters</h2><p>Both models have higher MAE than their baselines in the 2023 validation check. The 2024 improvement does not establish consistent superiority across years. For energy, the baseline also has lower 2024 RMSLE: the ranking depends on the error measure. Large reported outliers remain in the data and can dominate RMSE; no post-holdout outlier removal was used.</p></section>'
body+='<section><h2>Observed and predicted</h2><img src="model-diagnostics.png" alt="Actual R-generated holdout diagnostics and baseline comparison"></section>'
body+='<section><h2>Chronological evaluation</h2>'+table(BASE/'results/split-audit.csv')+'<p>The training row above describes the final refit. The 2023 validation population is inside that refit, but its reported score comes from an earlier model fitted only on data preceding 2023. The 2024 holdout remains outside both fits.</p></section>'
if (BASE/'results/row-flow.csv').exists():body+='<section><h2>Population and exclusions</h2>'+table(BASE/'results/row-flow.csv')+'</section>'
if (BASE/'results/quality-report.json').exists():
    q=json.loads((BASE/'results/quality-report.json').read_text());body+='<section><h2>Coverage audit</h2><pre>'+esc(json.dumps(q,indent=2))+'</pre></section>'
body+='<section><h2>Interpretation limits</h2><p>'+LIMITS+'</p><h3>Reproduce and inspect</h3><p>Open the included .Rproj in RStudio. Follow README.md to rerun the preparation and analysis, inspect coefficients, predictions, tests and saved model objects. The code uses base and recommended R packages; no package downloads or credentials are required.</p><a href="'+esc(manifest['landing_page'])+'">Official source and metadata</a></section><p class="footer">Independent portfolio demonstration using real public data. No fictional client outcomes. Code: MIT. Source data: City of Seattle, Public Domain per catalogue.</p>'
(BASE/'results/report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>'+TITLE+'</title><style>'+STYLE+'</style><main>'+body+'</main></html>')
print(comparison)
